[/list]
The full plan, with every test: [url=https://edgemodders.github.io/EDGEmat/]EDGEmat docs[/url].

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Questions[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Is this a game mod?[/b]
No. It's a tool for making mods, running in VS Code. It reads the game's files and never changes them. Your game doesn't need it.

[b]Can I recolor clothes with it now?[/b]
Yes. Change a layer's surface, color and finish, save it into your project, and pack it with REDcode. A layer can take the colors its surface offers; truly free colors are a later phase.

[b]Do the AI-made materials cost money?[/b]
Only what your image service charges you, with your own key: a few cents a take. EDGEmat never comes with a key and sends nothing until you press Generate. A photo of your own costs nothing.

[b]Do I need an AI or an account?[/b]
No. EDGEmat works fully on its own. The AI assistant is optional and uses your own Claude account; generating from words needs your own image service key.

[b]How is it different from MlsetupBuilder?[/b]
MlsetupBuilder is the editor many modders know, and EDGEmat learned from how it behaves. EDGEmat is a new editor written from scratch, in VS Code: it finds a garment's files from its name, describes layers in plain words, saves straight into a mod project with the meshes for both bodies, builds its library from your own game, makes materials from words, and works with AI assistants.

[b]Single-player only?[/b]
Yes. Cyberpunk 2077 is a single-player game, and EDGEmat is for single-player modding.

[b]Is it free?[/b]
Yes, and open source under the MIT license. The code is on [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/EDGEmat]GitHub[/url].

